                             LOST ON VENUS

In the Room of the Seven Doors, Carson Napier faced the choice of his
life. Six doors led to terrible deaths--the seventh was the door of
life. But for him, this door too would lead only to the new dangers
of a planet whose beasts were more frightful than those of his native
Earth.

But Carson sought the rescue of the planet's fairest princess, and even
though he stepped from one danger to meet another, he was determined to
make good an Earthman's pledge.

LOST ON VENUS is an Edgar Rice Burroughs adventure in the colorful and
exciting tradition of his Tarzan and Martian novels.


